WEBVTT

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.910
Found it.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.500
The cousin is shining.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.250
Huh?

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.710
You're shining.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.960
Sweat?

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.010
Must be nice.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.610
Tomorrow is the match that actually counts.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.240
It's what they're calling "the final showdown".

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.370
Is it?

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.200
Are you going to participate, transfer student?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.750
I'm not doing anything else, as usual, so I wouldn't mind.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.120
But we've lost every game so far.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.500
I don't think we stand a chance.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.340
Don't worry, those games didn't really count.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:37.170
What about Touwa?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.180
Are you playing baseball tomorrow, too?

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.430
She says she's going.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.930
Got it.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.060
There's also a <i>wonderful</i> surprise for tomorrow.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.440
It's not like we're having a talent show.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.360
See you tomorrow, then.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.110
Yeah.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.360
Cousin, wanna watch the stars?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.490
Oh...

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.460
If our growth each day were as discernible,

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:13.040
then our lives would be fun and have more purpose.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.880
According to Yashiro's logic,

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.590
it takes decades for a person to move a couple of centimeters.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.430
Isn't that discouraging?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:21.760
Tell me.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.850
Why do you play baseball?

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.440
S-Secret!

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:37.980
Fine.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.950
She claimed I had the potential.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:49.250
In other words, I have a chance at getting super powers.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.210
Where does she see such potential in me?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.920
Tiny steps forward that no one even notices...

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.970
I can't even reach that speed.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.250
I have to go get my card stamped.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.170
Let's get ready for the game.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.340
Let's!

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.840
All clean!

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.200
Not at all!
All clean!

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.490
The entire galaxy is crying over the suffering I endure at your hands.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.810
Thanks for waiting!

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.460
Here's your lunch.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.880
You've put a lot of effort into this.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.820
Gotta bring your own lunch for picnics!

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.190
I used to make huge feasts for Eri-chan!

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:12.640
There was so much food that I ended up eating for a whole day!

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:17.770
Well then,

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.230
off we go.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.400
Off! Off!

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.400
Go! Go!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.380
Maekawa's still in the restroom?

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.010
He must be nervous!

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:31.640
Hi there!

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.980
Yo, what's up?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.310
I came to cheer for you in return.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.570
Oh, you did?

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.690
Thanks...

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:48.450
Uh, Touwa-san...

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.450
Morning!

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.870
M-Mor...

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.620
Hey! Want to practice some more?

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.620
I will!

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.460
Here.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.460
Oh, thank you.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.960
Isn't this a catcher's mitt?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.630
Go for it, Niwa-kun!

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:11.550
Ryuushi-san, don't you have to support the city side?

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.220
It's Ryuuko!

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.890
Have you forgotten already?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:22.020
I'm always on <i>Niwa-kun's</i> side!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.740
You adolescent lovebirds!

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.830
Why are you mocking yourself too?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.540
Because I'm embarrassed!

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.040
I can't stay still!

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:46.260
Well, well. You're all early!

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.090
Ryuushi is here too.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.550
It's Ryuuko!

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.340
What's that, Maekawa-san?

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.510
Oh, it's a dugong.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.390
I'm a mermaid!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.350
By the way, we have an emergency.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.270
How is that a tone for an emergency?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.860
My father has succumbed to the pressure...

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.030
and run away.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:18.580
Who's going to pitch?

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.830
Who's ever pitched before?

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.080
I've played gateball.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.380
I've played billiards.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.000
Not all ball games are the same!

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:30.010
Testing, testing. Quiet down, everyone!

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.060
Mom!

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.350
What's with that getup?

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.730
This series was about to end without me playing a big role,

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.940
so I showed up on my own!

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.900
In video games not worth playing to the end,

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.990
final bosses should be this assertive,

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.370
or it's a waste of cool graphics!

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.700
Why is she here?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.700
She's the surprise.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.700
Too much of one...

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:01.910
That's how it is.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.290
I hired myself to be your beautiful coach.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.420
I'm going to get you motivated!

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.090
The delusions of the elderly are scary.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.090
All right, listen, guys.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.930
That's a coach for a different sport.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.680
Mako-kun's vulnerable to girls' scent.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.770
Make use of your socks to cover him.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.810
Are you trying to make me punch you?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.940
Question, coach.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.020
Mako-kun has become the guy who shares new information.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:32.820
Coach, you usually criticize the players during baseball games on TV,

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.570
but do you know the rules of baseball?

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:39.450
But I won't lose to anyone in passion!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:42.500
What part of your speech was passionate?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.290
You just rebelled against the coach, so Mako-kun is staying on the bench!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.750
In fact, you're staying on the chair!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.710
You monster!

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.630
More like a kid!

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:53.800
Coach, we have another problem.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.760
What is it, little part-timer?

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:59.560
We have an unprecedented pitcher shortage.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.180
My father ran away.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.100
Pitcher?

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.890
Why would you need a jug to play baseball?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.060
We don't need you on our team!

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.150
Okay, you're the pitcher, Eri-tan!

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.860
What?!

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.780
The coach's order is absolute!

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.280
All right!

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.280
Go line up!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.260
We will now begin the game.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.010
Bow!

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.800
Good luck!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.020
Erio really is the pitcher.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.190
The great match begins.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.110
Despair, adolescence, and the showcase of denpa...

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.830
hereby commence!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.160
However, Mako-kun was a bench warmer.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.040
What?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:08.040
What happened to the line between humor and seriousness?

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.000
Play ball!

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.130
So, what can you throw?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.590
A ball.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.140
No, I mean...

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:23.510
TV remote, pizza, dustcloth, book.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:27.020
Telescope... is too heavy.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:29.190
Let's do our best!

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.520
Yeah!

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.780
Are you seriously going to make me sit this out?

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:39.820
I want you to search for Maekawa-chan's father.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.120
There are only a few places he might be.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:45.740
The manga cafe by the station, the movie theater, or...

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.620
He's a habitual quitter?

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.080
Why me?

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.670
His own daughter would be far more convincing.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:57.420
I'm having Maekawa-chan play in your place.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.090
Besides, if you went...

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.050
If I went?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.850
It would be funnier, or so I've been told!

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.180
Hey...

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.220
Dissatisfied?

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.270
It's a hassle.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.100
Nothing I can do to persuade you?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.190
Pretty much.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.480
Everyone!

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:15.980
Mako-kun sniffed his auntie's scent from the futon she rolled in—

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.940
Fine, fine!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.200
Allow me to go search for him.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.450
I will never forgive that me from April.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:28.770
That's what I like about you, Mako-kun!

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:32.450
That's what makes my life a living hell.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.480
By the way, what happened to Miss Smooth Cheeks?

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.320
She seems to be pretty depressed.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:42.690
I came here to see Niwa-kun in action today.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.980
Don't worry.

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:48.810
I'm sure Mako-kun will come back and save the day when it really counts.

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:53.930
I sure hope so.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.670
Strike!

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.210
Eri-chan!

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:22.300
You're so cool!

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.430
Good luck.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.810
Since I can never become the hero of the story,

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.940
I continue to wriggle in the background.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:39.860
This is the search for Maekawa-san's missing father.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:43.530
On the other hand, it's also a reprieve granted to me.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:47.660
All I need to do is kill time searching, and wait until the game's over.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.200
Then I'll have the excuse of "unintended absence".

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.290
We're up against that Hanazawa-san girl.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.960
I'd just embarrass myself if I were there.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.960
If everything is decided in today's game,

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.880
Ryuushi-san won't have to come cheer for me again,

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.880
even if I don't show up for the rest of this game.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:09.510
You must have been relieved in that moment.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.980
Even if you got to play in the game,

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.270
could you possibly have performed well?

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:20.360
Wouldn't you just have embarrassed yourself in front of your parents?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.740
Isn't that right, Niwa-kun?

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:29.370
Yet I found myself pedaling the bicycle with all my might around the city,

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.990
hunting down Maekawa-san's father.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.910
Why are you following me?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.710
Because you're running.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:37.830
I'm not running!

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.420
I'm just on a journey to find myself!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:44.050
What can you possibly find in your own neighborhood?

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:52.140
This is more exhausting... than the game.

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.770
Same for me.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:58.150
Don't you have to play?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.270
I'm here because you ran away,

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.940
even though you're the ace pitcher.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.200
No way, I'm not going.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.910
That high school girl's too good.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.160
There's no way we can win.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.790
I pretty much agree.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.040
But they still make me pitch!

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:25.550
Not only that, it's the pitcher's fault for letting them score if we lose!

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.800
I'm sick of it!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.720
Your opposing pitcher is thinking the same thing.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:37.180
She told me her school team always loses.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.190
There's always someone better, huh?

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:48.530
She told me it's agonizing to pitch,

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:53.490
because she gives them false hopes of winning.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:56.410
That's an enviable problem to have.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.410
You can say that again.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:03.420
But I realized it's not such a bad problem.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:11.220
If you pitch, we'll at least have a glimpse of a hope of winning.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:16.680
Even if human beings can never fly on a bicycle,

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.680
I can't say for certain it's a bad thing

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.690
to make someone believe, "It may be possible to fly."

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:27.990
You're unmistakably the force behind our team.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:34.490
You may not have stood out, but you've played well.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:38.250
We haven't had a blowout loss so far.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.270
The protagonist.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:44.360
Someone the majority considers to be special.

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:45.900
The hero.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.240
I wanted to be one of those guys too.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:53.450
But it was too hard, so I gave up.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:56.980
To be honest, that's all there is to it.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.860
I've always been a quitter.

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.950
I stood my ground only three times in my life—
when I proposed to my wife,

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:17.240
when I thought about opening a bar,

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:21.370
and when I argued with my wife about my daughter's name.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.930
By the way,

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:38.810
what kind of friend are you to my daughter?

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.310
We're just cosplay friends.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.100
Liar!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:45.900
I'm going to make you come clean after the game, got it?

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.730
Uh... fine, fine.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.530
But I ran away.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.990
Everyone must be mad at me...

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.450
My arm's about to throw up.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:57.370
What kind of expression is that?

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.410
Don't worry!

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:04.920
A true hero always shows up in the nick of time.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.540
The game is already in the bottom of the fourth.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:13.630
The district side has runners on first and second from an error and a walk, with one out.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.430
You've done well.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.600
Change of plan, Meme-chin won't pinch hit.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.900
Sorry, we're late.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:28.900
Pinch hitter...

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:30.230
Mako-kun!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.480
Huh?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.730
Um...

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.990
You! You're up next inning, so your shoulder...

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.950
What were you supposed to do with it?

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:40.530
All right! Go spin it around!

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.290
I got it.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.580
Round and round!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.080
Meme-san.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.840
This is the critical moment in the game.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.670
Go and win it.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.730
Go for it!

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:08.980
Niwa-kun!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.770
Ow...

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.900
I'm so embarrassed!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:15.900
You should scream from farther away.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.740
What are you talking about?

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.780
It won't reach you unless I'm close to you!

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.330
Here.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.080
Okay.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.920
All right!

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.550
Good luck!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.920
Thanks!

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:44.010
In this moment slightly less dramatic than bases loaded with two outs,

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:50.270
believing in the 0.00000000198 cm/s of remote possibility...

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:52.770
Once again...

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:55.070
this time around...

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.400
I'll blast out a home run!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.250
Hoshimiya Yashiro,

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:10.210
I'll take on this challenge without giving up!

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.880
I don't have any super powers,

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:20.510
so I can only make do with what I have.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.390
The first pitch is my only chance.

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:26.260
It'll be a straight ball, low, down the middle.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:29.230
It's Hanazawa-san's favorite spot.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:33.230
I didn't strike out about twenty times for nothing!

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:36.730
Her first pitch usually ends up there!

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.780
That's my only chance.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:45.950
There it is!

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:50.290
It'll be too late by the time I see the ball and swing.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.710
I have no talent for baseball, given my poor hand-eye coordination.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.550
But this one time, just once,

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:59.050
please give me the result even if I lack talent!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.010
I've swung late again,

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:03.260
but I connect with it like a claw ripping through flesh,

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:05.350
like a death grip of a handshake!

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:07.260
Like a person spending his whole life...

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:10.100
covering the last centimeter to his goal!

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.990
I... did it?

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.250
The cousin!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.380
The ball is...

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.930
My hands are numb.

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:51.640
I've given my all, yet...

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.570
What the...

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:13.870
I will hope... and pray...

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.790
for those last few centimeters.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:19.840
For the miraculous blessing brought to me at a turtle's pace!

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:50.870
It didn't go the direction I intended it to.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.990
What, are you blushing?

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.500
Transfer student?

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:59.250
Ni... Niwa-kun is Mr. Miracle, starting today!

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.920
What?

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:06.260
There're still the fifth and the final innings remaining in the game,

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:08.640
but it's all right.

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:11.010
We'll definitely win!

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:12.390
Right?

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:19.350
It seems we have a chance at winning, so I'll pitch to win.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:23.280
And... don't forget our little talk, about my daughter.

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:28.490
The cousin is so cool!

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:30.990
Thank you.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.920
That was a great call. I'm such a talented coach!

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:40.670
You're not supposed to say it yourself.

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:45.090
That's why you get a reward from the goddess!

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:48.930
"Goddess" is short for "<i>god</i>-like <i>des</i>truction"?

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:55.390
The world calls this a kiss or something...

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:04.020
Wh-What?

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:04.820
Woo.

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.530
You two sound so fake!

00:25:16.990 --> 00:25:18.950
First Home Run of my life: +4

00:25:18.950 --> 00:25:21.050
First kiss being accidental: -5

00:25:21.050 --> 00:25:23.580
Current adolescence points total: + 18

00:25:23.820 --> 00:25:26.130
Next time: Midnight Sun.

00:25:26.130 --> 00:25:28.990
The heart of summer holidays, the night of the festival.

00:25:28.990 --> 00:25:35.300
I thought it was a good way to wait for the end, bathing in a bright amber light like this.

00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:39.760
However, the mystery around that esper girl still remains.

00:25:39.760 --> 00:25:41.410
What difference would believing make?

00:25:41.410 --> 00:25:43.480
Remember the difference with all your five senses!

00:25:43.480 --> 00:25:45.530
The story's not over yet.
